1
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:04,125
Part two: Escalation of Pain

2
00:00:04,833 --> 00:00:08,291
When pain gets worse: Pinpointing the pain

3
00:00:08,666 --> 00:00:11,000
Sometimes the pain can get worse

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,875
and spread
to different parts of your head and neck.

5
00:00:14,125 --> 00:00:18,666
When this happens, it is important
to tell us exactly where it hurts.

6
00:00:18,666 --> 00:00:21,333
That way,
we can give treatment that targets

7
00:00:21,333 --> 00:00:24,333
the painful area to help make it better.

8
00:00:24,958 --> 00:00:27,750
Pain in the Neck, Ear or Nerves:

9
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:29,541
Gabapentin

10
00:00:29,541 --> 00:00:31,791
If the pain follows a nerve

11
00:00:31,791 --> 00:00:35,125
and affects your neck, ears,
or other areas of the face,

12
00:00:35,541 --> 00:00:38,750
we might give you a medicine
called gabapentin.

13
00:00:38,958 --> 00:00:42,958
This medicine is specifically useful
in targeting nerve pain,

14
00:00:42,958 --> 00:00:47,125
and it is not an opioid,
so it has fewer side effects.

15
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:52,875
Once we start gabapentin, we can adjust
the dose to help manage the level of pain.

16
00:00:53,291 --> 00:00:56,500
Gabapentin can cause sleepiness or nausea,

17
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:01,541
so we recommend taking the medication
at night before bedtime to start with.

18
00:01:01,541 --> 00:01:03,083
If tolerated well,

19
00:01:03,083 --> 00:01:07,458
you can increase the dose
and also take it more throughout the day.

20
00:01:07,958 --> 00:01:10,541
Using Opioid Pain Pills

21
00:01:11,041 --> 00:01:13,125
For about half of the patients,

22
00:01:13,125 --> 00:01:17,458
opioid pain medications might be needed
by the end of treatment.

23
00:01:17,583 --> 00:01:20,416
These include liquid morphine rinses

24
00:01:20,416 --> 00:01:24,458
or pills like hydrocodone or oxycodone.

25
00:01:24,708 --> 00:01:28,625
We try to save these strong medicines
for when you really need them.

26
00:01:28,958 --> 00:01:33,041
Don't hesitate to ask for them
if your pain is too much to handle.

27
00:01:33,416 --> 00:01:36,416
We can help you find the right dose
to manage your pain.

28
00:01:36,916 --> 00:01:42,125
We will discuss side effects and safety
of these medications in a separate video.

29
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:45,500
Getting Help from Pain Management
Specialists.

30
00:01:45,791 --> 00:01:48,708
If you're trying lots of things
and still in pain,

31
00:01:48,958 --> 00:01:51,708
we can get help from pain management
specialists.

32
00:01:51,958 --> 00:01:54,666
Let us know
if your pain isn't getting better

33
00:01:54,666 --> 00:01:56,666
and we can involve them sooner.

34
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,875
If you were already in pain
before starting treatment,

35
00:02:00,083 --> 00:02:03,250
we can even get them involved right away.
